WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.210 --> 00:00:06.620
Let's go to the phone lines at six one seven
eight three zero forty seven fifty.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:10.160
Starting today with our caller from the two
seven zero area code.

00:00:10.160 --> 00:00:11.220
Caller from two seven zero.

00:00:11.220 --> 00:00:12.220
What's your name?

00:00:12.220 --> 00:00:14.019
Where are you calling from?

00:00:14.019 --> 00:00:19.499
Western Kentucky, you said Damon from western
Kentucky.

00:00:19.499 --> 00:00:20.499
Go ahead.

00:00:20.499 --> 00:00:21.499
Yes, sir.

00:00:21.499 --> 00:00:22.499
Well, I was just calling.

00:00:22.499 --> 00:00:25.429
First of all, I want to point out I'm sorry.

00:00:25.429 --> 00:00:27.159
I'm kind of nervous here.

00:00:27.159 --> 00:00:28.159
That's OK.

00:00:28.159 --> 00:00:31.800
But Biden and Harris are not my first choice
at all.

00:00:31.800 --> 00:00:32.829
OK, thank you.

00:00:32.829 --> 00:00:36.629
I think the worse worse you could've gotten,
that would have been Biden Clow, which are

00:00:36.629 --> 00:00:37.629
OK.

00:00:37.629 --> 00:00:39.370
After a little bit of agonizing.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:45.499
I decided I am voting Biden just because even
though I'm in Kentucky and I think if I voted

00:00:45.499 --> 00:00:47.300
third party, it wouldn't matter much anyways.

00:00:47.300 --> 00:00:52.789
I want to see Trump lose big in the popular
vote just so he can't say, oh, this was rigged.

00:00:52.789 --> 00:00:57.730
I think there really needs to be a great big
coalition rejecting him.

00:00:57.730 --> 00:00:58.730
I agree.

00:00:58.730 --> 00:01:02.559
I mentioned this last week in that we have
to run up the score.

00:01:02.559 --> 00:01:05.810
Obviously, this is an Electoral College contest.

00:01:05.810 --> 00:01:11.270
But given that, we anticipate Donald Trump
might either try to challenge the results

00:01:11.270 --> 00:01:16.140
or claim it was rigged or whatever, a bigger
margin in the popular vote is better than

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:17.140
a smaller margin.

00:01:17.140 --> 00:01:18.140
So I agree with you.

00:01:18.140 --> 00:01:19.140
Exactly.

00:01:19.140 --> 00:01:23.920
I didn't want to say as you more Morgus pragmatic,
left leaning people.

00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:28.009
I do think one way we can screw up is we don't
need the same people.

00:01:28.009 --> 00:01:29.009
Yes.

00:01:29.009 --> 00:01:30.009
Feel different.

00:01:30.009 --> 00:01:33.600
We need to explain to them this is the best
description I ever heard.

00:01:33.600 --> 00:01:34.950
And forgive for going on too long.

00:01:34.950 --> 00:01:35.950
Make this quick.

00:01:35.950 --> 00:01:41.110
There is a left wing YouTube who said if you
believe in what Bernie and what AOC stand

00:01:41.110 --> 00:01:46.700
for and you look at the amount of work they
put in and what they fought for.

00:01:46.700 --> 00:01:51.000
If you think, oh, we're just going to punt
this and let Trump get it because right.

00:01:51.000 --> 00:01:54.740
Get the right president, you pretty much helping
destroy everything they work for.

00:01:54.740 --> 00:02:00.100
Because I don't think Biden is necessarily
going to become progressive when he gets elected,

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:03.369
but it's going to be a lot easier to convince
him and Harris

00:02:03.369 --> 00:02:09.300
to go for Medicare for all and go for free
college and legalizing marijuana.

00:02:09.300 --> 00:02:10.300
It is Trump.

00:02:10.300 --> 00:02:14.700
And I think we have to understand that and
we have to look at the down ballot votes and

00:02:14.700 --> 00:02:21.060
we have to look at this as a way of, for lack
of a better term, helping to infiltrate the

00:02:21.060 --> 00:02:22.060
Democratic Party.

00:02:22.060 --> 00:02:24.040
Well, that sounds really Machiavellian.

00:02:24.040 --> 00:02:26.031
Well, but it makes sense.

00:02:26.031 --> 00:02:29.890
And I think, you know, Matt, you and I don't
think we're going to get Medicare for all

00:02:29.890 --> 00:02:34.000
because not because of Biden, but because
most Democratic senators don't even support

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.000
it.

00:02:35.000 --> 00:02:36.180
But that's a that's a specific thing.

00:02:36.180 --> 00:02:41.260
You're completely right that with Trump, we
get zero percent of what Bernie wanted.

00:02:41.260 --> 00:02:47.570
And with Biden, we probably definitely get
10 percent and are in a position to get another

00:02:47.570 --> 00:02:48.570
50 percent.

00:02:48.570 --> 00:02:49.870
I mean, listen, it's just numbers, right?

00:02:49.870 --> 00:02:55.230
And so the only real argument would be I want
to destroy the entire system, to build it

00:02:55.230 --> 00:02:57.780
back up in the image that I value.

00:02:57.780 --> 00:03:01.820
But there's no historical example that tells
us that's how change happens.

00:03:01.820 --> 00:03:04.030
So I would reject it on historical grounds.

00:03:04.030 --> 00:03:07.340
But you and I, I think, are on the same page,
of course.

00:03:07.340 --> 00:03:09.840
And one more thing and then I'll let Bob stop.

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:14.620
I started with Cornel West, and I think the
best thing he said is he said basically implied

00:03:14.620 --> 00:03:16.990
he's going to vote for Biden and Harris.

00:03:16.990 --> 00:03:20.040
But he said that does not mean I endorse them.

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.880
That does not mean that I'm not going to criticize
them.

00:03:21.880 --> 00:03:27.310
And I think we need to be able to point out
when they do something wrong.

00:03:27.310 --> 00:03:29.840
Just like I remember when your your big Bernie
supporter.

00:03:29.840 --> 00:03:34.880
But when Bernie did something you thought
was the wrong thing, you would not pay by

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:36.370
it, right?

00:03:36.370 --> 00:03:37.370
Yeah.

00:03:37.370 --> 00:03:38.370
I mean, listen.

00:03:38.370 --> 00:03:42.040
All that voting for one person over another
means is you think you're better than that

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.040
other.

00:03:43.040 --> 00:03:44.270
Do you think they are better than that other
person?

00:03:44.270 --> 00:03:45.600
That's all that I mean, it doesn't mean anything
else.

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:48.610
And then we go and we do do the work.

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:50.300
All right, my friend, thank you for the call.

00:03:50.300 --> 00:03:51.150
I appreciate it.

